Not if you choose the right items to polypile. Seriously, in my last
game, I got an amulets of life saving, rings of levitation, free
action, and conflict, five scrolls of enchant weapon, two scrolls of
enchant armor, a scroll of charging, and jumping boots *from a single
round of polypiling*. That's usual for me.

Polypiling sucks if you want a single item, say, a cloak of magic
resistance, or a single scroll type such as charging or genocide. But
if your kit has big gaping holes in it, polypiling has good odds of
filling *some* of those holes. And polypiling scrolls gives *tons* of
blessed identify scrolls, which make the equipment you already have
much more useful. If I have a choice of sacrificing some burdensome
junk that would go in a stash/BoH now, or completing my kit post-
castle later, what's the disadvantage in polypiling now?

> You have not even worked your way thru the lowest levels yet? You'll
> find many useful items there.

You will also find zruties, boss liches, minotaurs, and dragons down
there, not to mention "it looks rather muddy down here" deathtraps.
Polypiling isn't necessary by any means, but it can give an early-game
character a big advantage if used wisely. And *early* is when cool
stuff like gauntlets of power and amulets of reflection actually make
a difference.


